<rml>
<head>
	<!-- The closed chat's lines (P11 spec D4): the newest four lines for 5 s
	     above the taskbar, on the view shade, in a document of their own, so
	     an appended line lays out this small document and not the whole
	     chat. While the chat is closed and shown, the facade
	     nui_chat.ChatWindow shows this board (nui_chat_view.ChatViewBoard,
	     controller assets/root/nui_chat_view.py) and the chat document's
	     lines element is off; while the chat is open, this board hides. The
	     body is the chat's 600dp block, placed by the facade where it places
	     the chat (its bottom center on the taskbar's top). It takes no
	     pointer but on its links and never the focus; a press on a link sends
	     nuilink, which the chat facade turns into the legacy item tooltip,
	     or with left Alt a paste. The view-chat option hides the lines. -->
	<title>chat-view</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="chat-view.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="chat-view nui-below-legacy-ui" data-model="chat_view">
	<div id="chat-view" class="chat-view__block" data-class-is-quiet="!view_chat">
		<nui-chat-lines id="chat-view-lines" class="chat__lines" view="window" step="15" mode="view" data-event-nuilink="link(ev.link)"/>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
